			"notes": "## What's changed in 1.4.3\n\n### Blurred vignette (bodycam periphery)\n- New **Vignette Blur** slider in the Post-FX tab (`0.0`–`1.0`, default `0.6`).\n- The vignette is now applied **before** the defocus pass, and each of the 12 golden-angle taps re-applies the vignette at its own position — so the dark contour genuinely bleeds into the image, like a real bodycam periphery, instead of ending on a clean, sharp curve.\n- Edge mask starts earlier and reaches ~53 px at the frame corner at full strength.\n\n### The black frame border now melts\n- The fisheye crop no longer ends on a razor-sharp cut. Outside the valid sample area the frame keeps sampling through a defocus disc that grows with the distance out, then fades to black.\n- Width scales with the **Vignette Blur** slider — set it to `0` to get the old hard cut back.\n\n### Config screen auto-save\n- Every slider and toggle is written to disk the moment you change it, and survives `ESC` (previously only the *Save* button persisted changes).\n\n---\n\n**Minecraft 1.20.1 · Fabric · client-side only.** Drop the jar in `mods/`.\n\nSource, issues and wiki: https://github.com/jhfuheuiwfh/nexus-bodycam-mod\n\n**AI disclosure:** Mostly ai-generated code and assets, with some user-made code!"
